{"book":26,"chapter":30,"context":{"chapter":30,"title":"The Day of Egypt","summary":"A lament announces the 'day of the LORD' on Egypt and its allies, naming city after city, and declares that God has broken Pharaoh's arm while strengthening Babylon's.","background":"The cities named span Egypt: Noph (Memphis), No (Thebes), Sin (Pelusium), Aven (Heliopolis), Pi-beseth (Bubastis), Tehaphnehes (Tahpanhes), Zoan (Tanis) and Pathros (southern Egypt). The 'broken arm' oracle (vv. 20–26) is dated a few months before Jerusalem fell; many connect it with Egypt's failed attempt to break Babylon's siege.","customs":[{"term":"Arm","verses":"30:21-25","note":"In Egyptian royal art Pharaoh often raised a mighty arm to strike enemies. Ezekiel's image of a broken arm that cannot hold a sword turns that boast upside down."}],"watchFor":["The 'day of the LORD' turned against a foreign nation (v. 3).","The contrast of arms: Pharaoh's broken, Babylon's strengthened (vv. 24–25)."],"connections":["Jeremiah 37:5-7","Jeremiah 43:8-13","Joel 2:1-2"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it came"],["דְבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]]},"2":{"w":[["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","O son of"],["אָדָם","'adam","H120","HNcmsa","humankind"],["הִנָּבֵא","hinave'","H5012","HVNv2ms","prophesy"],["וְאָמַרְתָּ","ve'amarta","H559","Hc/Vqq2ms","and you will say"],["כֹּה","koh","H3541","HD","thus"],["אָמַר","'amar","H559","HVqp3ms","he says"],["אֲדֹנָי","'adonai","H136","HNpt","[the] Lord"],["יְהוִה","yahweh","H3069","HNpt","Yahweh"],["הֵילִילוּ","heililu","H3213","HVhv2mp","wail"],["הָהּ","hah","H1929","HTj","alas!"],["לַיּוֹם","laiyom","H3117","HRd/Ncmsa","for the day"]],"x":[[23013006,23013006,5],[23015002,23015002,3],[26021012,26021012,3],[29001005,29001005,3],[29001011,29001011,3]],"xn":5},"3":{"w":[["כִּי","ki-","H3588","